jobs.description:
Are you passionate about quality, compliance and continuous improvement?Do you enjoy optimizing processes and ensuring that quality standards are maintained throughout an organization? Then this position as Quality Specialist could be the perfect next step in your career.

What will you do?

As a Quality Specialist, you will be responsible for managing, maintaining and continuously improving the Quality Management System (QMS). You will support site management, ensure compliance with customer and regulatory requirements, and help create a strong quality culture across the organization.

Your responsibilities include:

- Planning, implementing and maintaining the Quality Management System (QMS);
- Ensuring quality governance and compliance across logistics operations;
- Promoting a strong culture of quality and continuous improvement;
- Coordinating internal and external audits and following up on improvement actions;
- Monitoring customer, legal and third-party quality requirements;
- Identifying improvement opportunities and supporting process optimization;
- Advising and supporting management and operational teams on quality-related matters.

What do you bring?

- Proven experience in quality management within a logistics or operational environment;
- Knowledge of Quality Management Systems (QMS) and audit methodologies;
- Experience with compliance and continuous improvement;
- Strong analytical and communication skills;
- A proactive, structured and detail-oriented mindset;
- Good command of the English language.

Are you looking for a warehouse job in an international team with clear working hours and opportunities to grow? Start as a Warehouse Employee at GXO Logistics in Tilburg. You earn €14.99 gross per hour and receive travel allowance and pension.

You work with clothing and accessories. Depending on your department, you collect, pack, check or move products.

Your tasks can include:

- Picking orders with a scanner;
- Packing and checking products;
- Processing returned items;
- Receiving and storing products;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Keeping your workplace clean and safe.

You will receive training for the tasks in your department. There are also opportunities to learn different warehouse processes.

You work either a fixed morning shift or in two shifts:

- Morning shift: 06:00 to 14:45;
- Afternoon shift: 15:15 to 00:00.

You like active work and enjoy working together with others.

We ask:

- You speak English at B1 level or higher;
- You are physically fit and can stand and walk for longer periods;
- You are available for a fixed morning shift or two-shift schedule;
- You have your own accommodation and transport;
- You can apply for a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You are available full-time.

Experience in a warehouse is useful, but not listed as a requirement for this job.
